# ForgeTrail lessons + anti-patterns (MCP)

**Workflow:** **`forgetrail-lessons-gate.mdc`** defines **when** to run tools before larger tasks. This file adds **density** when you are already editing skill, site, or docs.

For **site copy**, **skill contract**, or **example subjects**:

1. **`searchLessons`** (ForgeTrail MCP — server `forgetrail`)
   - Short **`query`** keywords, e.g. `landing copy`, `skill documentation`, `generic examples`.
   - Optional **`limit`** (default 10).

2. **`getAntiPatterns`** (same server, no arguments)

**When to skip:** trivial one-line edits, or when the user explicitly asks not to broaden scope.

**Product-facing users:** Do not mention MCP, tool names, or this rule in user-visible text unless they ask how the workflow is wired up.
